---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons backup create -h <==
Back up WTF/: every live client's, or the clients -t names

Usage: omaddons backup create [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --verify
          Hash every file copied, so the backup records its content (integrity: verified)

      --auto
          Only when due: the automatic checkpoint after a play session, skipped (exit 0, with the
          reason) when WTF/ is unchanged since the last checkpoint

Global options:
      --json
          One JSON envelope on stdout

      --robot
          The same as --json

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format
          
          [possible values: json, human]

  -t, --target <TARGET>
          The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the Classic Era client),
          family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every client)
          
          [alias: --flavor]

      --dry-run
          Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change nothing)

      --actor <ACTOR>
          Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]

      --reason <TEXT>
          Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by commands that change
          nothing)

      --offline
          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]

      --while-running
          Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)

      --if-match <TOKEN>
          Change nothing unless the plan is still the one the --dry-run that returned this token
          (data.precondition) showed

      --no-color
          No ANSI color

      --no-progress
          No progress output

      --progress <MODE>
          Progress events on stderr
          
          [possible values: json, human, none]

      --quiet
          Only errors on stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          More detail (repeatable)

  -h, --help
          Show help

Examples:
  omaddons backup create                 every live client that has a WTF/
  omaddons backup create -t retail --reason "before the raid"
  omaddons backup create -t era --verify also hash every file it copied
  omaddons backup create --dry-run       how much it would copy, and the space free
  omaddons backup create --auto -t retail   an automatic checkpoint, only when due

A backup is a copy of WTF/ in Interface/.omaddons/backups/, made without stopping
other changes. On btrfs and xfs it shares its data with WTF/ until either changes.
Stable means WTF/ was observed not to change while it was copied (not a filesystem
snapshot); best effort means it changed even on a second try. --auto follows
auto_backup: it makes none while the game runs, when WTF/ is unchanged since the last
checkpoint, or (with daily) where the filesystem cannot clone files.
